[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The systems table's sources cell splits on commas, and a space fails silently

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SYSTEMS-SOURCES-SPLIT-ON-COMMAS
TITLE: The systems table's sources cell splits on commas, and a space fails silently
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
queries._split_words splits the systems table's sources cell on COMMAS, not on
whitespace, despite its name. A space-separated cell parses as one unmatchable
prefix, silently unholding every directory in that row.

Measured 2026-08-31: adding a second source to the core row with a space
unheld both that plan and strictdoc-tooling. view-check's systems-table rule
caught it, which is the only reason it was not committed -- and that rule is
not in nix flake check, so the same mistake lands green in CI.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MECH-BACKLOG-WHITEBOARD-VIEW
  ROLE: Backlogged_In
